Thanks Mike for answering and for spotting the underscore issue.

Note that for the new GENEActiv 1.2 model ActivInsights has informed me that the lux values have a different non-linear output coding. They plan to provide me with more specific instructions to handle this, which I can then embed in GGIR or GGIRread accordingly. I have a few test recordings for which the light peak values seem plausible, so this is not easy to spot.

Best regards,

Vincent

On Thursday, 29 February 2024 at 3:52 PM, Michael Rueschman <michael....@gmail.com> wrote:

> Misia,
>
> The epoch-by-epoch output, which includes a lightpeak column with lux values, is located in /output_folder/meta/ms5.outraw
>
> In that folder you'll find a "behavioralcodes" CSV file and then another folder (I think the name depends upon activity thresholds) that contains 1 epoch-by-epoch CSV per recording.
>
> Importantly, I think you need to fix your ms5-related configuration options to use an underscore (e.g., save_ms5rawlevels) instead of a period (e.g., save.ms5rawlevels in your code snippet above).
